# global: the partition every context lands in unless it names another, and the
# one an unconfigured mux uses. Shipped, so discovery works out of the box;
# override it by dropping your own in $MUX_DIR/partitions/.
#
# `scan` is here rather than in mux's built-in defaults ON PURPOSE. Built-ins
# carry behaviour only, never a location, so a partition nobody configured gets
# no roots and therefore no map -- which is how a missing context file makes
# itself visible instead of quietly indexing the wrong tree.
scan    ~/src 3
